# tally 2.1.7 S4 (#131): a recurrence reading two of its own cells, fib[n] = fib[n - 1] + fib[n - 2]: the chain
# follows the first cell each step reads that nothing has printed (c6 .. c2); fib[c4], which fib[c6] reads too, was
# a folded step, so it prints where next met, folding its own chain (c4, c3, c1). The layout is this interpreter's.
# Was (2.1.6): every step printed.
=== f.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
index cnt = [c1, c2, c3, c4, c5, c6]
input one: int

def fib[n in cnt]: int = if pos(n) <= 2 then one else fib[n - 1] + fib[n - 2]

ask e: explain fib[c6]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  one = 1 "s"
=== expect
e: 8
  [1] fib[c6] = 8
      rule base: won
        … 3 more steps of fib, c5 .. c3 …
        [2] fib[c2] = 1
            rule base: won
              [3] row v:one = 1
                  version v, source s, "s", locator "s", governs always, known 2026-01-01
        … 2 more steps of fib, c4 .. c3 …
        [4] fib[c1] = 1
            rule base: won
              (v:one: see [3])
  cut 2026-10-18
